---The settings in JSON format for the DMS Transfer type source endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.DmsTransferSettings
---@field ServiceAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) used by the service access IAM role. The role must allow the iam:PassRole action.
---@field BucketName? aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the S3 bucket to use.

---Provides information that defines a DocumentDB data provider.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.DocDbDataProviderSettings
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the source DocumentDB server.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The port value for the DocumentDB data provider.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String The database name on the DocumentDB data provider.
---@field SslMode? aws.database_migration_service.DmsSslModeValue|string The SSL mode used to connect to the DocumentDB data provider. The default value is none.
---@field CertificateArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the certificate used for SSL connection.

---Provides information that defines a DocumentDB endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.DocDbSettings
---@field Username? aws.database_migration_service.String The user name you use to access the DocumentDB source endpoint.
---@field Password? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret The password for the user account you use to access the DocumentDB source endpoint.
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the server on the DocumentDB source endpoint.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The port value for the DocumentDB source endpoint.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String The database name on the DocumentDB source endpoint.
---@field NestingLevel? aws.database_migration_service.NestingLevelValue|string Specifies either document or table mode.
---@field ExtractDocId? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the document ID is added to the target table. Use this setting when NestingLevel is set to "none".
---@field DocsToInvestigate? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Indicates the number of documents to preview to determine the document organization. Use this setting when NestingLevel is set to "one".
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.database_migration_service.String The KMS key identifier that is used to encrypt the content on the replication instance. If you don't specify a value for the KmsKeyId parameter, then DMS uses your default encryption key. KMS creates the default encryption key for your Amazon Web Services account. Your Amazon Web Services account has a different default encryption key for each Amazon Web Services Region.
---@field SecretsManagerAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The full Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IAM role that specifies DMS as the trusted entity and grants the required permissions to access the value in SecretsManagerSecret. The role must allow the iam:PassRole action. SecretsManagerSecret has the value of the Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager secret that allows access to the DocumentDB endpoint.
---@field SecretsManagerSecretId? aws.database_migration_service.String The full ARN, partial ARN, or friendly name of the SecretsManagerSecret that contains the DocumentDB endpoint connection details.
---@field UseUpdateLookUp? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional If true, DMS retrieves the entire document from the DocumentDB source during migration. This may cause a migration failure if the server response exceeds bandwidth limits. To fetch only updates and deletes during migration, set this parameter to false.
---@field ReplicateShardCollections? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional If true, DMS replicates data to shard collections. DMS only uses this setting if the target endpoint is a DocumentDB elastic cluster.

---@alias aws.database_migration_service.DoubleOptional number

---Provides the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Identity and Access Management (IAM) role used to define an Amazon DynamoDB target endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.DynamoDbSettings
---@field ServiceAccessRoleArn aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) used by the service to access the IAM role. The role must allow the iam:PassRole action.

---Provides information that defines an OpenSearch endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.ElasticsearchSettings
---@field ServiceAccessRoleArn aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) used by the service to access the IAM role. The role must allow the iam:PassRole action.
---@field EndpointUri aws.database_migration_service.String The endpoint for the OpenSearch cluster. DMS uses HTTPS if a transport protocol (http/https) is not specified.
---@field FullLoadErrorPercentage? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The maximum percentage of records that can fail to be written before a full load operation stops.
---@field ErrorRetryDuration? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The maximum number of seconds for which DMS retries failed API requests to the OpenSearch cluster.
---@field UseNewMappingType? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this option to true for DMS to migrate documentation using the documentation type _doc. OpenSearch and an Elasticsearch cluster only support the _doc documentation type in versions 7. x and later. The default value is false.

---@alias aws.database_migration_service.EncodingTypeValue "plain"|"plain-dictionary"|"rle-dictionary"

---@alias aws.database_migration_service.EncryptionModeValue "sse-s3"|"sse-kms"

---Describes an endpoint of a database instance in response to operations such as the following:
---@class aws.database_migration_service.Endpoint
---@field EndpointIdentifier? aws.database_migration_service.String The database endpoint identifier. Identifiers must begin with a letter and must contain only ASCII letters, digits, and hyphens. They can't end with a hyphen or contain two consecutive hyphens.
---@field EndpointType? aws.database_migration_service.ReplicationEndpointTypeValue The type of endpoint. Valid values are source and target.
---@field EngineName? aws.database_migration_service.String The database engine name. Valid values, depending on the EndpointType, include "mysql", "oracle", "postgres", "mariadb", "aurora", "aurora-postgresql", "redshift", "redshift-serverless", "s3", "db2", "db2-zos", "azuredb", "sybase", "dynamodb", "mongodb", "kinesis", "kafka", "elasticsearch", "documentdb", "sqlserver", "neptune", and "babelfish".
---@field EngineDisplayName? aws.database_migration_service.String The expanded name for the engine name. For example, if the EngineName parameter is "aurora", this value would be "Amazon Aurora MySQL".
---@field Username? aws.database_migration_service.String The user name used to connect to the endpoint.
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the server at the endpoint.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The port value used to access the endpoint.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the database at the endpoint.
