---Provides information that describes an Apache Kafka endpoint. This information includes the output format of records applied to the endpoint and details of transaction and control table data information.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.KafkaSettings
---@field Broker? aws.database_migration_service.String A comma-separated list of one or more broker locations in your Kafka cluster that host your Kafka instance. Specify each broker location in the form broker-hostname-or-ip:port . For example, "ec2-12-345-678-901.compute-1.amazonaws.com:2345". For more information and examples of specifying a list of broker locations, see Using Apache Kafka as a target for Database Migration Service in the Database ...
---@field Topic? aws.database_migration_service.String The topic to which you migrate the data. If you don't specify a topic, DMS specifies "kafka-default-topic" as the migration topic.
---@field MessageFormat? aws.database_migration_service.MessageFormatValue|string The output format for the records created on the endpoint. The message format is JSON (default) or JSON_UNFORMATTED (a single line with no tab).
---@field IncludeTransactionDetails? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Provides detailed transaction information from the source database. This information includes a commit timestamp, a log position, and values for transaction_id, previous transaction_id, and transaction_record_id (the record offset within a transaction). The default is false.
---@field IncludePartitionValue? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Shows the partition value within the Kafka message output unless the partition type is schema-table-type. The default is false.
---@field PartitionIncludeSchemaTable? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Prefixes schema and table names to partition values, when the partition type is primary-key-type. Doing this increases data distribution among Kafka partitions. For example, suppose that a SysBench schema has thousands of tables and each table has only limited range for a primary key. In this case, the same primary key is sent from thousands of tables to the same partition, which causes throttling...
---@field IncludeTableAlterOperations? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Includes any data definition language (DDL) operations that change the table in the control data, such as rename-table, drop-table, add-column, drop-column, and rename-column. The default is false.
---@field IncludeControlDetails? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Shows detailed control information for table definition, column definition, and table and column changes in the Kafka message output. The default is false.
---@field MessageMaxBytes? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The maximum size in bytes for records created on the endpoint The default is 1,000,000.
---@field IncludeNullAndEmpty? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Include NULL and empty columns for records migrated to the endpoint. The default is false.
---@field SecurityProtocol? aws.database_migration_service.KafkaSecurityProtocol|string Set secure connection to a Kafka target endpoint using Transport Layer Security (TLS). Options include ssl-encryption, ssl-authentication, and sasl-ssl. sasl-ssl requires SaslUsername and SaslPassword.
---@field SslClientCertificateArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the client certificate used to securely connect to a Kafka target endpoint.
---@field SslClientKeyArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the client private key used to securely connect to a Kafka target endpoint.
---@field SslClientKeyPassword? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret The password for the client private key used to securely connect to a Kafka target endpoint.
---@field SslCaCertificateArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the private certificate authority (CA) cert that DMS uses to securely connect to your Kafka target endpoint.
---@field SaslUsername? aws.database_migration_service.String The secure user name you created when you first set up your MSK cluster to validate a client identity and make an encrypted connection between server and client using SASL-SSL authentication.
---@field SaslPassword? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret The secure password you created when you first set up your MSK cluster to validate a client identity and make an encrypted connection between server and client using SASL-SSL authentication.
---@field NoHexPrefix? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this optional parameter to true to avoid adding a '0x' prefix to raw data in hexadecimal format. For example, by default, DMS adds a '0x' prefix to the LOB column type in hexadecimal format moving from an Oracle source to a Kafka target. Use the NoHexPrefix endpoint setting to enable migration of RAW data type columns without adding the '0x' prefix.
---@field SaslMechanism? aws.database_migration_service.KafkaSaslMechanism|string For SASL/SSL authentication, DMS supports the SCRAM-SHA-512 mechanism by default. DMS versions 3.5.0 and later also support the PLAIN mechanism. To use the PLAIN mechanism, set this parameter to PLAIN.
---@field SslEndpointIdentificationAlgorithm? aws.database_migration_service.KafkaSslEndpointIdentificationAlgorithm|string Sets hostname verification for the certificate. This setting is supported in DMS version 3.5.1 and later.
---@field UseLargeIntegerValue? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Specifies using the large integer value with Kafka.

---@alias aws.database_migration_service.KafkaSslEndpointIdentificationAlgorithm "none"|"https"

