---@class aws.database_migration_service.ModifyReplicationTaskMessage
---@field ReplicationTaskArn aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the replication task.
---@field ReplicationTaskIdentifier? aws.database_migration_service.String The replication task identifier.
---@field MigrationType? aws.database_migration_service.MigrationTypeValue|string The migration type. Valid values: full-load | cdc | full-load-and-cdc
---@field TableMappings? aws.database_migration_service.String When using the CLI or boto3, provide the path of the JSON file that contains the table mappings. Precede the path with file://. For example, --table-mappings file://mappingfile.json. When working with the DMS API, provide the JSON as the parameter value.
---@field ReplicationTaskSettings? aws.database_migration_service.String JSON file that contains settings for the task, such as task metadata settings.
---@field CdcStartTime? aws.database_migration_service.TStamp Indicates the start time for a change data capture (CDC) operation. Use either CdcStartTime or CdcStartPosition to specify when you want a CDC operation to start. Specifying both values results in an error.
---@field CdcStartPosition? aws.database_migration_service.String Indicates when you want a change data capture (CDC) operation to start. Use either CdcStartPosition or CdcStartTime to specify when you want a CDC operation to start. Specifying both values results in an error.
---@field CdcStopPosition? aws.database_migration_service.String Indicates when you want a change data capture (CDC) operation to stop. The value can be either server time or commit time.
---@field TaskData? aws.database_migration_service.String Supplemental information that the task requires to migrate the data for certain source and target endpoints. For more information, see Specifying Supplemental Data for Task Settings in the Database Migration Service User Guide.

---@class aws.database_migration_service.ModifyReplicationTaskResponse
---@field ReplicationTask? aws.database_migration_service.ReplicationTask The replication task that was modified.

---Provides information that defines a MongoDB data provider.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.MongoDbDataProviderSettings
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the MongoDB server.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The port value for the MongoDB data provider.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String The database name on the MongoDB data provider.
---@field SslMode? aws.database_migration_service.DmsSslModeValue|string The SSL mode used to connect to the MongoDB data provider. The default value is none.
---@field CertificateArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the certificate used for SSL connection.
---@field AuthType? aws.database_migration_service.AuthTypeValue|string The authentication type for the database connection. Valid values are PASSWORD or NO.
---@field AuthSource? aws.database_migration_service.String The MongoDB database name. This setting isn't used when AuthType is set to "no".
---@field AuthMechanism? aws.database_migration_service.AuthMechanismValue|string The authentication method for connecting to the data provider. Valid values are DEFAULT, MONGODB_CR, or SCRAM_SHA_1.

---Provides information that defines a MongoDB endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.MongoDbSettings
---@field Username? aws.database_migration_service.String The user name you use to access the MongoDB source endpoint.
---@field Password? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret The password for the user account you use to access the MongoDB source endpoint.
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the server on the MongoDB source endpoint. For MongoDB Atlas, provide the server name for any of the servers in the replication set.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The port value for the MongoDB source endpoint.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String The database name on the MongoDB source endpoint.
---@field AuthType? aws.database_migration_service.AuthTypeValue|string The authentication type you use to access the MongoDB source endpoint.
---@field AuthMechanism? aws.database_migration_service.AuthMechanismValue|string The authentication mechanism you use to access the MongoDB source endpoint.
---@field NestingLevel? aws.database_migration_service.NestingLevelValue|string Specifies either document or table mode.
---@field ExtractDocId? aws.database_migration_service.String Specifies whether the document ID is added to the target table. Use this setting when NestingLevel is set to "none".
---@field DocsToInvestigate? aws.database_migration_service.String Indicates the number of documents to preview to determine the document organization. Use this setting when NestingLevel is set to "one".
---@field AuthSource? aws.database_migration_service.String The MongoDB database name. This setting isn't used when AuthType is set to "no".
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.database_migration_service.String The KMS key identifier that is used to encrypt the content on the replication instance. If you don't specify a value for the KmsKeyId parameter, then DMS uses your default encryption key. KMS creates the default encryption key for your Amazon Web Services account. Your Amazon Web Services account has a different default encryption key for each Amazon Web Services Region.
---@field SecretsManagerAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The full Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IAM role that specifies DMS as the trusted entity and grants the required permissions to access the value in SecretsManagerSecret. The role must allow the iam:PassRole action. SecretsManagerSecret has the value of the Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager secret that allows access to the MongoDB endpoint.
---@field SecretsManagerSecretId? aws.database_migration_service.String The full ARN, partial ARN, or friendly name of the SecretsManagerSecret that contains the MongoDB endpoint connection details.
---@field UseUpdateLookUp? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional If true, DMS retrieves the entire document from the MongoDB source during migration. This may cause a migration failure if the server response exceeds bandwidth limits. To fetch only updates and deletes during migration, set this parameter to false.
---@field ReplicateShardCollections? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional If true, DMS replicates data to shard collections. DMS only uses this setting if the target endpoint is a DocumentDB elastic cluster.

---@class aws.database_migration_service.MoveReplicationTaskMessage
---@field ReplicationTaskArn aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the task that you want to move.
---@field TargetReplicationInstanceArn aws.database_migration_service.String The ARN of the replication instance where you want to move the task to.

---@class aws.database_migration_service.MoveReplicationTaskResponse
---@field ReplicationTask? aws.database_migration_service.ReplicationTask The replication task that was moved.

---@alias aws.database_migration_service.MySQLAuthenticationMethod "password"|"iam"

---Provides information that defines a MySQL endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.MySQLSettings
---@field AfterConnectScript? aws.database_migration_service.String Specifies a script to run immediately after DMS connects to the endpoint. The migration task continues running regardless if the SQL statement succeeds or fails.
---@field CleanSourceMetadataOnMismatch? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Cleans and recreates table metadata information on the replication instance when a mismatch occurs. For example, in a situation where running an alter DDL on the table could result in different information about the table cached in the replication instance.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String Database name for the endpoint. For a MySQL source or target endpoint, don't explicitly specify the database using the DatabaseName request parameter on either the CreateEndpoint or ModifyEndpoint API call. Specifying DatabaseName when you create or modify a MySQL endpoint replicates all the task tables to this single database. For MySQL endpoints, you specify the database only when you specify th...
---@field EventsPollInterval? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Specifies how often to check the binary log for new changes/events when the database is idle. The default is five seconds.
---@field TargetDbType? aws.database_migration_service.TargetDbType|string Specifies where to migrate source tables on the target, either to a single database or multiple databases. If you specify SPECIFIC_DATABASE, specify the database name using the DatabaseName parameter of the Endpoint object.
---@field MaxFileSize? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Specifies the maximum size (in KB) of any .csv file used to transfer data to a MySQL-compatible database.
---@field ParallelLoadThreads? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Improves performance when loading data into the MySQL-compatible target database. Specifies how many threads to use to load the data into the MySQL-compatible target database. Setting a large number of threads can have an adverse effect on database performance, because a separate connection is required for each thread. The default is one.
---@field Password? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret Endpoint connection password.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Endpoint TCP port.
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String The host name of the endpoint database.
---@field ServerTimezone? aws.database_migration_service.String Specifies the time zone for the source MySQL database.
---@field Username? aws.database_migration_service.String Endpoint connection user name.
---@field SecretsManagerAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The full Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IAM role that specifies DMS as the trusted entity and grants the required permissions to access the value in SecretsManagerSecret. The role must allow the iam:PassRole action. SecretsManagerSecret has the value of the Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager secret that allows access to the MySQL endpoint.
---@field SecretsManagerSecretId? aws.database_migration_service.String The full ARN, partial ARN, or friendly name of the SecretsManagerSecret that contains the MySQL endpoint connection details.
---@field ExecuteTimeout? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Sets the client statement timeout (in seconds) for a MySQL source endpoint.
---@field ServiceAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The IAM role you can use to authenticate when connecting to your endpoint. Ensure to include iam:PassRole and rds-db:connect actions in permission policy.
---@field AuthenticationMethod? aws.database_migration_service.MySQLAuthenticationMethod|string This attribute allows you to specify the authentication method as "iam auth".

---Provides information that defines a MySQL data provider.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.MySqlDataProviderSettings
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the MySQL server.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The port value for the MySQL data provider.
---@field SslMode? aws.database_migration_service.DmsSslModeValue|string The SSL mode used to connect to the MySQL data provider. The default value is none.
---@field CertificateArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the certificate used for SSL connection.
---@field S3Path? aws.database_migration_service.String The path for the Amazon S3 bucket that the application uses for accessing the user-defined schema.
---@field S3AccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The ARN for the role the application uses to access its Amazon S3 bucket.

---Provides information that defines an Amazon Neptune endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.NeptuneSettings
---@field ServiceAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the service role that you created for the Neptune target endpoint. The role must allow the iam:PassRole action. For more information, see Creating an IAM Service Role for Accessing Amazon Neptune as a Target in the Database Migration Service User Guide.
---@field S3BucketName aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the Amazon S3 bucket where DMS can temporarily store migrated graph data in .csv files before bulk-loading it to the Neptune target database. DMS maps the SQL source data to graph data before storing it in these .csv files.
---@field S3BucketFolder aws.database_migration_service.String A folder path where you want DMS to store migrated graph data in the S3 bucket specified by S3BucketName
---@field ErrorRetryDuration? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The number of milliseconds for DMS to wait to retry a bulk-load of migrated graph data to the Neptune target database before raising an error. The default is 250.
---@field MaxFileSize? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The maximum size in kilobytes of migrated graph data stored in a .csv file before DMS bulk-loads the data to the Neptune target database. The default is 1,048,576 KB. If the bulk load is successful, DMS clears the bucket, ready to store the next batch of migrated graph data.
---@field MaxRetryCount? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The number of times for DMS to retry a bulk load of migrated graph data to the Neptune target database before raising an error. The default is 5.
---@field IamAuthEnabled? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional If you want Identity and Access Management (IAM) authorization enabled for this endpoint, set this parameter to true. Then attach the appropriate IAM policy document to your service role specified by ServiceAccessRoleArn. The default is false.

---@alias aws.database_migration_service.NestingLevelValue "none"|"one"

---@alias aws.database_migration_service.OracleAuthenticationMethod "password"|"kerberos"

---Provides information that defines an Oracle data provider.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.OracleDataProviderSettings
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String The name of the Oracle server.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The port value for the Oracle data provider.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String The database name on the Oracle data provider.
---@field SslMode? aws.database_migration_service.DmsSslModeValue|string The SSL mode used to connect to the Oracle data provider. The default value is none.
---@field CertificateArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the certificate used for SSL connection.
---@field AsmServer? aws.database_migration_service.String The address of your Oracle Automatic Storage Management (ASM) server. You can set this value from the asm_server value. You set asm_server as part of the extra connection attribute string to access an Oracle server with Binary Reader that uses ASM. For more information, see Configuration for change data capture (CDC) on an Oracle source database.
---@field SecretsManagerOracleAsmSecretId? aws.database_migration_service.String The identifier of the secret in Secrets Manager that contains the Oracle ASM connection details.
---@field SecretsManagerOracleAsmAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The ARN of the IAM role that provides access to the secret in Secrets Manager that contains the Oracle ASM connection details.
---@field SecretsManagerSecurityDbEncryptionSecretId? aws.database_migration_service.String The identifier of the secret in Secrets Manager that contains the transparent data encryption (TDE) password. DMS requires this password to access Oracle redo logs encrypted by TDE using Binary Reader.
---@field SecretsManagerSecurityDbEncryptionAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The ARN of the IAM role that provides access to the secret in Secrets Manager that contains the TDE password.
---@field S3Path? aws.database_migration_service.String The path for the Amazon S3 bucket that the application uses for accessing the user-defined schema.
---@field S3AccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The ARN for the role the application uses to access its Amazon S3 bucket.

---Provides information that defines an Oracle endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.OracleSettings
---@field AddSupplementalLogging? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to set up table-level supplemental logging for the Oracle database. This attribute enables PRIMARY KEY supplemental logging on all tables selected for a migration task.
---@field ArchivedLogDestId? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Specifies the ID of the destination for the archived redo logs. This value should be the same as a number in the dest_id column of the v$archived_log view. If you work with an additional redo log destination, use the AdditionalArchivedLogDestId option to specify the additional destination ID. Doing this improves performance by ensuring that the correct logs are accessed from the outset.
---@field AdditionalArchivedLogDestId? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Set this attribute with ArchivedLogDestId in a primary/ standby setup. This attribute is useful in the case of a switchover. In this case, DMS needs to know which destination to get archive redo logs from to read changes. This need arises because the previous primary instance is now a standby instance after switchover.
---@field ExtraArchivedLogDestIds? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerList Specifies the IDs of one more destinations for one or more archived redo logs. These IDs are the values of the dest_id column in the v$archived_log view. Use this setting with the archivedLogDestId extra connection attribute in a primary-to-single setup or a primary-to-multiple-standby setup.
---@field AllowSelectNestedTables? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to true to enable replication of Oracle tables containing columns that are nested tables or defined types.
---@field ParallelAsmReadThreads? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Set this attribute to change the number of threads that DMS configures to perform a change data capture (CDC) load using Oracle Automatic Storage Management (ASM). You can specify an integer value between 2 (the default) and 8 (the maximum). Use this attribute together with the readAheadBlocks attribute.
---@field ReadAheadBlocks? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Set this attribute to change the number of read-ahead blocks that DMS configures to perform a change data capture (CDC) load using Oracle Automatic Storage Management (ASM). You can specify an integer value between 1000 (the default) and 200,000 (the maximum).
---@field AccessAlternateDirectly? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to false in order to use the Binary Reader to capture change data for an Amazon RDS for Oracle as the source. This tells the DMS instance to not access redo logs through any specified path prefix replacement using direct file access.
---@field UseAlternateFolderForOnline? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to true in order to use the Binary Reader to capture change data for an Amazon RDS for Oracle as the source. This tells the DMS instance to use any specified prefix replacement to access all online redo logs.
---@field OraclePathPrefix? aws.database_migration_service.String Set this string attribute to the required value in order to use the Binary Reader to capture change data for an Amazon RDS for Oracle as the source. This value specifies the default Oracle root used to access the redo logs.
---@field UsePathPrefix? aws.database_migration_service.String Set this string attribute to the required value in order to use the Binary Reader to capture change data for an Amazon RDS for Oracle as the source. This value specifies the path prefix used to replace the default Oracle root to access the redo logs.
---@field ReplacePathPrefix? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to true in order to use the Binary Reader to capture change data for an Amazon RDS for Oracle as the source. This setting tells DMS instance to replace the default Oracle root with the specified usePathPrefix setting to access the redo logs.
---@field EnableHomogenousTablespace? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to enable homogenous tablespace replication and create existing tables or indexes under the same tablespace on the target.
---@field DirectPathNoLog? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When set to true, this attribute helps to increase the commit rate on the Oracle target database by writing directly to tables and not writing a trail to database logs.
---@field ArchivedLogsOnly? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When this field is set to True, DMS only accesses the archived redo logs. If the archived redo logs are stored on Automatic Storage Management (ASM) only, the DMS user account needs to be granted ASM privileges.
---@field AsmPassword? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret For an Oracle source endpoint, your Oracle Automatic Storage Management (ASM) password. You can set this value from the asm_user_password value. You set this value as part of the comma-separated value that you set to the Password request parameter when you create the endpoint to access transaction logs using Binary Reader. For more information, see Configuration for change data capture (CDC) on an...
---@field AsmServer? aws.database_migration_service.String For an Oracle source endpoint, your ASM server address. You can set this value from the asm_server value. You set asm_server as part of the extra connection attribute string to access an Oracle server with Binary Reader that uses ASM. For more information, see Configuration for change data capture (CDC) on an Oracle source database.
---@field AsmUser? aws.database_migration_service.String For an Oracle source endpoint, your ASM user name. You can set this value from the asm_user value. You set asm_user as part of the extra connection attribute string to access an Oracle server with Binary Reader that uses ASM. For more information, see Configuration for change data capture (CDC) on an Oracle source database.
---@field CharLengthSemantics? aws.database_migration_service.CharLengthSemantics|string Specifies whether the length of a character column is in bytes or in characters. To indicate that the character column length is in characters, set this attribute to CHAR. Otherwise, the character column length is in bytes.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String Database name for the endpoint.
---@field DirectPathParallelLoad? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When set to true, this attribute specifies a parallel load when useDirectPathFullLoad is set to Y. This attribute also only applies when you use the DMS parallel load feature. Note that the target table cannot have any constraints or indexes.
---@field FailTasksOnLobTruncation? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When set to true, this attribute causes a task to fail if the actual size of an LOB column is greater than the specified LobMaxSize.
---@field NumberDatatypeScale? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Specifies the number scale. You can select a scale up to 38, or you can select FLOAT. By default, the NUMBER data type is converted to precision 38, scale 10.
---@field Password? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret Endpoint connection password.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Endpoint TCP port.
---@field ReadTableSpaceName? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When set to true, this attribute supports tablespace replication.
---@field RetryInterval? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Specifies the number of seconds that the system waits before resending a query.
---@field SecurityDbEncryption? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret For an Oracle source endpoint, the transparent data encryption (TDE) password required by DMS to access Oracle redo logs encrypted by TDE using Binary Reader. It is also the TDE_Password part of the comma-separated value you set to the Password request parameter when you create the endpoint. The SecurityDbEncryption setting is related to this SecurityDbEncryptionName setting. For more information,...
---@field SecurityDbEncryptionName? aws.database_migration_service.String For an Oracle source endpoint, the name of a key used for the transparent data encryption (TDE) of the columns and tablespaces in an Oracle source database that is encrypted using TDE. The key value is the value of the SecurityDbEncryption setting. For more information on setting the key name value of SecurityDbEncryptionName, see the information and example for setting the securityDbEncryptionNam...
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String Fully qualified domain name of the endpoint.
---@field SpatialDataOptionToGeoJsonFunctionName? aws.database_migration_service.String Use this attribute to convert SDO_GEOMETRY to GEOJSON format. By default, DMS calls the SDO2GEOJSON custom function if present and accessible. Or you can create your own custom function that mimics the operation of SDOGEOJSON and set SpatialDataOptionToGeoJsonFunctionName to call it instead.
---@field StandbyDelayTime? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Use this attribute to specify a time in minutes for the delay in standby sync. If the source is an Oracle Active Data Guard standby database, use this attribute to specify the time lag between primary and standby databases.
---@field Username? aws.database_migration_service.String Endpoint connection user name.
---@field UseBFile? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to True to capture change data using the Binary Reader utility. Set UseLogminerReader to False to set this attribute to True. To use Binary Reader with Amazon RDS for Oracle as the source, you set additional attributes. For more information about using this setting with Oracle Automatic Storage Management (ASM), see Using Oracle LogMiner or DMS Binary Reader for CDC.
---@field UseDirectPathFullLoad? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to True to have DMS use a direct path full load. Specify this value to use the direct path protocol in the Oracle Call Interface (OCI). By using this OCI protocol, you can bulk-load Oracle target tables during a full load.
---@field UseLogminerReader? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to True to capture change data using the Oracle LogMiner utility (the default). Set this attribute to False if you want to access the redo logs as a binary file. When you set UseLogminerReader to False, also set UseBfile to True. For more information on this setting and using Oracle ASM, see Using Oracle LogMiner or DMS Binary Reader for CDC in the DMS User Guide.
---@field SecretsManagerAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The full Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IAM role that specifies DMS as the trusted entity and grants the required permissions to access the value in SecretsManagerSecret. The role must allow the iam:PassRole action. SecretsManagerSecret has the value of the Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager secret that allows access to the Oracle endpoint.
---@field SecretsManagerSecretId? aws.database_migration_service.String The full ARN, partial ARN, or friendly name of the SecretsManagerSecret that contains the Oracle endpoint connection details.
---@field SecretsManagerOracleAsmAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String Required only if your Oracle endpoint uses Automatic Storage Management (ASM). The full ARN of the IAM role that specifies DMS as the trusted entity and grants the required permissions to access the SecretsManagerOracleAsmSecret. This SecretsManagerOracleAsmSecret has the secret value that allows access to the Oracle ASM of the endpoint.
---@field SecretsManagerOracleAsmSecretId? aws.database_migration_service.String Required only if your Oracle endpoint uses Automatic Storage Management (ASM). The full ARN, partial ARN, or friendly name of the SecretsManagerOracleAsmSecret that contains the Oracle ASM connection details for the Oracle endpoint.
---@field TrimSpaceInChar? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Use the TrimSpaceInChar source endpoint setting to trim data on CHAR and NCHAR data types during migration. The default value is true.
---@field ConvertTimestampWithZoneToUTC? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When true, converts timestamps with the timezone datatype to their UTC value.
---@field OpenTransactionWindow? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional The timeframe in minutes to check for open transactions for a CDC-only task.
---@field AuthenticationMethod? aws.database_migration_service.OracleAuthenticationMethod|string Specifies the authentication method to be used with Oracle.

