---Provides information that defines a PostgreSQL endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.PostgreSQLSettings
---@field AfterConnectScript? aws.database_migration_service.String For use with change data capture (CDC) only, this attribute has DMS bypass foreign keys and user triggers to reduce the time it takes to bulk load data.
---@field CaptureDdls? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional To capture DDL events, DMS creates various artifacts in the PostgreSQL database when the task starts. You can later remove these artifacts.
---@field MaxFileSize? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Specifies the maximum size (in KB) of any .csv file used to transfer data to PostgreSQL.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String Database name for the endpoint.
---@field DdlArtifactsSchema? aws.database_migration_service.String The schema in which the operational DDL database artifacts are created.
---@field ExecuteTimeout? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Sets the client statement timeout for the PostgreSQL instance, in seconds. The default value is 60 seconds.
---@field FailTasksOnLobTruncation? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When set to true, this value causes a task to fail if the actual size of a LOB column is greater than the specified LobMaxSize.
---@field HeartbeatEnable? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional The write-ahead log (WAL) heartbeat feature mimics a dummy transaction. By doing this, it prevents idle logical replication slots from holding onto old WAL logs, which can result in storage full situations on the source. This heartbeat keeps restart_lsn moving and prevents storage full scenarios.
---@field HeartbeatSchema? aws.database_migration_service.String Sets the schema in which the heartbeat artifacts are created.
---@field HeartbeatFrequency? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Sets the WAL heartbeat frequency (in minutes).
---@field Password? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret Endpoint connection password.
---@field Port? aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Endpoint TCP port. The default is 5432.
---@field ServerName? aws.database_migration_service.String The host name of the endpoint database.
---@field Username? aws.database_migration_service.String Endpoint connection user name.
---@field SlotName? aws.database_migration_service.String Sets the name of a previously created logical replication slot for a change data capture (CDC) load of the PostgreSQL source instance.
---@field PluginName? aws.database_migration_service.PluginNameValue|string Specifies the plugin to use to create a replication slot.
---@field SecretsManagerAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The full Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IAM role that specifies DMS as the trusted entity and grants the required permissions to access the value in SecretsManagerSecret. The role must allow the iam:PassRole action. SecretsManagerSecret has the value of the Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager secret that allows access to the PostgreSQL endpoint.
---@field SecretsManagerSecretId? aws.database_migration_service.String The full ARN, partial ARN, or friendly name of the SecretsManagerSecret that contains the PostgreSQL endpoint connection details.
---@field TrimSpaceInChar? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Use the TrimSpaceInChar source endpoint setting to trim data on CHAR and NCHAR data types during migration. The default value is true.
---@field MapBooleanAsBoolean? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When true, lets PostgreSQL migrate the boolean type as boolean. By default, PostgreSQL migrates booleans as varchar(5). You must set this setting on both the source and target endpoints for it to take effect.
---@field MapJsonbAsClob? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When true, DMS migrates JSONB values as CLOB.
---@field MapLongVarcharAs? aws.database_migration_service.LongVarcharMappingType|string Sets what datatype to map LONG values as.
---@field DatabaseMode? aws.database_migration_service.DatabaseMode|string Specifies the default behavior of the replication's handling of PostgreSQL- compatible endpoints that require some additional configuration, such as Babelfish endpoints.
---@field BabelfishDatabaseName? aws.database_migration_service.String The Babelfish for Aurora PostgreSQL database name for the endpoint.
---@field DisableUnicodeSourceFilter? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Disables the Unicode source filter with PostgreSQL, for values passed into the Selection rule filter on Source Endpoint column values. By default DMS performs source filter comparisons using a Unicode string which can cause look ups to ignore the indexes in the text columns and slow down migrations.
---@field ServiceAccessRoleArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The IAM role arn you can use to authenticate the connection to your endpoint. Ensure to include iam:PassRole and rds-db:connect actions in permission policy.
---@field AuthenticationMethod? aws.database_migration_service.PostgreSQLAuthenticationMethod|string This attribute allows you to specify the authentication method as "iam auth".

---Provides information that defines a PostgreSQL data provider.
