---Provides information that defines a Redis target endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.RedisSettings
---@field ServerName aws.database_migration_service.String Fully qualified domain name of the endpoint.
---@field Port aws.database_migration_service.Integer Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) port for the endpoint.
---@field SslSecurityProtocol? aws.database_migration_service.SslSecurityProtocolValue|string The connection to a Redis target endpoint using Transport Layer Security (TLS). Valid values include plaintext and ssl-encryption. The default is ssl-encryption. The ssl-encryption option makes an encrypted connection. Optionally, you can identify an Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for an SSL certificate authority (CA) using the SslCaCertificateArn setting. If an ARN isn't given for a CA, DMS uses the ...
---@field AuthType? aws.database_migration_service.RedisAuthTypeValue|string The type of authentication to perform when connecting to a Redis target. Options include none, auth-token, and auth-role. The auth-token option requires an AuthPassword value to be provided. The auth-role option requires AuthUserName and AuthPassword values to be provided.
---@field AuthUserName? aws.database_migration_service.String The user name provided with the auth-role option of the AuthType setting for a Redis target endpoint.
---@field AuthPassword? aws.database_migration_service.SecretString|distilled.Secret The password provided with the auth-role and auth-token options of the AuthType setting for a Redis target endpoint.
---@field SslCaCertificateArn? aws.database_migration_service.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the certificate authority (CA) that DMS uses to connect to your Redis target endpoint.

