---Provides information that defines an Amazon Timestream endpoint.
---@class aws.database_migration_service.TimestreamSettings
---@field DatabaseName aws.database_migration_service.String Database name for the endpoint.
---@field MemoryDuration aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Set this attribute to specify the length of time to store all of the tables in memory that are migrated into Amazon Timestream from the source database. Time is measured in units of hours. When Timestream data comes in, it first resides in memory for the specified duration, which allows quick access to it.
---@field MagneticDuration aws.database_migration_service.IntegerOptional Set this attribute to specify the default magnetic duration applied to the Amazon Timestream tables in days. This is the number of days that records remain in magnetic store before being discarded. For more information, see Storage in the Amazon Timestream Developer Guide.
---@field CdcInsertsAndUpdates? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to true to specify that DMS only applies inserts and updates, and not deletes. Amazon Timestream does not allow deleting records, so if this value is false, DMS nulls out the corresponding record in the Timestream database rather than deleting it.
---@field EnableMagneticStoreWrites? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional Set this attribute to true to enable memory store writes. When this value is false, DMS does not write records that are older in days than the value specified in MagneticDuration, because Amazon Timestream does not allow memory writes by default. For more information, see Storage in the Amazon Timestream Developer Guide.

---@alias aws.database_migration_service.TlogAccessMode "BackupOnly"|"PreferBackup"|"PreferTlog"|"TlogOnly"

---@class aws.database_migration_service.UpdateSubscriptionsToEventBridgeMessage
---@field ForceMove? aws.database_migration_service.BooleanOptional When set to true, this operation migrates DMS subscriptions for Amazon SNS notifications no matter what your replication instance version is. If not set or set to false, this operation runs only when all your replication instances are from DMS version 3.4.5 or higher.

---@class aws.database_migration_service.UpdateSubscriptionsToEventBridgeResponse
---@field Result? aws.database_migration_service.String A string that indicates how many event subscriptions were migrated and how many remain to be migrated.

